<title>UK: Reed bounces after Wednesday's weakness.</title>
<headline>Reed bounces after Wednesday's weakness.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Reed International Plc pushed ahead on Thursday after a poor performance Wednesday, bucking the weaker market trend, dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock put on 7-1/2p to 585p by 1327 GMT, having shed 13p on Wednesday. Nearly 1.3 million shares changed hands.</p>
<p>&quot;There was a badly handled sell order yesterday which doesn't appear to be around today,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>Others said they had not seen the sell order and saw no particular reason for Reed to rise.</p>
<p>-- Louise Ireland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
